{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"agent_message","text":"**Library Files**\nThe implementation wired by [test5.mjs](/output/test5.mjs) is split across these `.mjs` modules in `/output`:\n\n- [lib/cli/spec.mjs](/output/lib/cli/spec.mjs) for the option spec plus exact usage/help/error text.\n- [lib/cli/parser.mjs](/output/lib/cli/parser.mjs) for manual `process.argv` parsing with argparse-like behavior, required `int` validation, `--help`, `--help=...`, `--`, duplicate flags, and underscore-containing integers.\n- [lib/graph/digraph.mjs](/output/lib/graph/digraph.mjs) for a minimal directed graph implementation.\n- [lib/graph/dag.mjs](/output/lib/graph/dag.mjs) for directed-acyclic-graph detection.\n- [lib/format/python.mjs](/output/lib/format/python.mjs) for Python-style boolean formatting (`True` / `False`).\n- [lib/index.mjs](/output/lib/index.mjs) for local ESM re-exports.\n\n**Entry File**\n[test5.mjs](/output/test5.mjs)\n\n```js\nimport {\n  DiGraph,\n  formatPythonBool,\n  getProgramName,\n  isDirectedAcyclicGraph,\n  parseTest5Arguments,\n} from './lib/index.mjs';\n\nconst programName = getProgramName(process.argv[1]);\nconst parsedArguments = parseTest5Arguments(process.argv.slice(2), programName);\n\nif (parsedArguments.kind === 'help') {\n  process.stdout.write(parsedArguments.text);\n  process.exit(0);\n}\n\nif (parsedArguments.kind === 'error') {\n  process.stderr.write(parsedArguments.text);\n  process.exit(parsedArguments.code);\n}\n\nconst { a, b, c, d, e } = parsedArguments.values;\nconst graph = new DiGraph();\n\ngraph.addEdgesFrom([\n  [a, b],\n  [b, c],\n  [c, d],\n  [d, e],\n]);\n\nprocess.stdout.write(`${formatPythonBool(isDirectedAcyclicGraph(graph))}\\n`);\n```\n\nVerified against `/workspace/dataset/test5_executable` for valid input, cyclic input, missing required args, invalid ints, unknown args, help output, `--help=1`, `--` handling, duplicate flags, and underscore-form integers."}}
